WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:03.870
I’m a long time iPhone user and the last
time I was intrigued enough to personally

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:09.139
buy a Samsung device was the S7 edge but when
the S10 devices were announced, like many

00:00:09.139 --> 00:00:15.419
of you I was intrigued.

00:00:15.419 --> 00:00:24.150
Now we obviously have a tech channel here
on Youtube so we were going to pick one up

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:28.000
but I wanted to give this beautiful device
a chance to win over a permanent spot in my

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:29.000
pocket.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.529
Its been a month now and I’ll be honest,
yes I did switch back to iPhone XS Max.

00:00:32.529 --> 00:00:37.070
I’ll let you know why soon, but first let
me tell you everything I love about the S10+

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:38.730
and the things that really annoyed me.

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:43.000
Let me start out with the best thing that
no one is talking about, the LTE speeds.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:48.460
I don’t know if it's just my network, my
city, or what but wow what a difference.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:54.170
I tested it around town and the S10+ routinely
gets twice the LTE speed than my XS Max and

00:00:54.170 --> 00:00:57.190
at least 1 extra bar in tough areas.

00:00:57.190 --> 00:01:00.690
This isn’t just in benchmarks, but I noticed
it every day.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:06.360
Everything loads faster, buffering is minimized,
and I can reliably stream 1440P video where

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.760
my iPhone would hang up at 1080P.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:13.299
If you’re an iPhone user struggling with
reception, this alone may be a reason to switch.

00:01:13.299 --> 00:01:18.630
The S10+ is an amazing device and a big step
ahead of the Pixel 3, One Plus 6T and other

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.700
Androids.

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:23.460
Comparing the hardware with the iPhone flagships,
it’s definitely the more impressive device.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:27.020
Samsung has made great strides over the S9
and Note 9.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:29.910
I didn’t think they could make the display
any better but they did.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.780
Battery life was good, now it's better.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:34.950
We didn’t have a notch before, and we still
don’t.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:39.090
The cutout is much less intrusive even from
day one, even the pill shaped one.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:42.580
When you put this thing up to the iPhone it
looks like the future, and it puts the Pixel

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.580
3 to shame.

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:48.770
I do wish it didn’t have the depth sensor
and retained the s10’s circular cutout,

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.299
but that's a minor complaint.

00:01:50.299 --> 00:01:52.160
On the back, we now have three cameras.

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.310
I LOVE that we have a wide angle lens.

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:58.659
The quality isn’t as good as the main shooter,
but the perspective it provides is very unique.

00:01:58.659 --> 00:02:02.970
The distortion is surprisingly minimal due
to software correction and for most people

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:07.110
even those who have actual cameras, this will
be wider than other lenses they own.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:12.310
I own 7 cameras and dozens of lenses but use
my phone more often because it's always there

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:14.599
so camera quality matters a lot to me.

00:02:14.599 --> 00:02:18.750
This means I always try to own the best smartphone
camera available and through the years that's

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:19.840
been the iPhone.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:23.260
Switching to the Samsung, I wasn’t giving
up quality like in the past.

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:27.700
In our own blind comparison, The S10+ beat
out the iPhone overall, and watching Zone

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:31.311
of Techs comparison, I chose the iPhone as
my preference but the S10+ was very close,

00:02:31.311 --> 00:02:32.540
and comparing it to the note 9 you can see
how huge of an improvement was made in just

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:33.540
6 months.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:37.910
There are three things that bugged me, first,
Panoramas are now shot using the wide angle.

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:41.200
This gives you a different perspective but
can really mess up your images.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.690
Second, for portraits, you have to use the
standard lens.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:49.280
This is great to show more of your science
and helps in low light, but Samsung is the

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:51.110
king of giving us options.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:55.280
Why not let us choose which lens is better
for a particular situation, both for Portraits

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.540
and Panoramas.

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.319
The third is the shutter lag.

00:02:58.319 --> 00:03:04.819
Apple was able to fix this since its a12 processor
is constantly taking a bunch of images which

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:07.800
does introduce more noise but you never miss
a shot.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:13.180
The S10+ at times can have close to a second
of delay so I did miss some shots of my kids

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:14.900
that I wouldn’t have with the iPhone.

00:03:14.900 --> 00:03:18.570
As far as the video and mic quality, they
have also made great strides but from my pro

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:29.629
videographer perspective, the overall quality
is still behind Apple.

00:03:29.629 --> 00:03:34.459
Stabilization is great, and the super smooth
video is really cool but it's limited to 1080P.

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:39.319
Almost no reviewer mentioned the HDR10+ feature
and that's because it's not really usable

00:03:39.319 --> 00:03:44.519
for most if you want to edit and upload HDR,
mostly only good if you want to rewatch on

00:03:44.519 --> 00:03:45.769
the phone itself.

00:03:45.769 --> 00:03:50.581
One features I miss is 24FPS recording on
the iPhone which helps in low light and is

00:03:50.581 --> 00:03:53.210
great if you want to match with other camera
footage.

00:03:53.210 --> 00:03:56.850
Speakers have always been a weak point for
Samsung, but not anymore.

00:03:56.850 --> 00:04:00.441
The S10+ doesn’t sound as good as the iPhone,
and yes I did enable Dolby Atmos, but it's

00:04:00.441 --> 00:04:12.990
close and much louder.

00:04:12.990 --> 00:04:18.219
I would choose the S10’s speakers any day
since the extra volume comes in really handy

00:04:18.219 --> 00:04:21.299
when listening to a podcast or video that's
too quiet.

00:04:21.299 --> 00:04:25.889
Speaking of watching videos, oh man, the experience
is fantastic.

00:04:25.889 --> 00:04:30.110
Not only is the HDR both brighter and more
contrasty, but the higher rez display with

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:34.749
the ability to stream 1440P instead of 1080P
really makes the image pop.

00:04:34.749 --> 00:04:40.039
Not only that, but the small cutout is way
less noticeable, and I flip the phone so it's

00:04:40.039 --> 00:04:41.039
at the bottom right.

00:04:41.039 --> 00:04:43.479
With the iPhone, I almost never went full
screen because of the notch, but here that's

00:04:43.479 --> 00:04:44.479
a non-issue.

00:04:44.479 --> 00:04:47.499
That better video viewing experience also
drains more of the battery, but since the

00:04:47.499 --> 00:04:52.689
S10+ has a larger battery, I still got 30min
to an hour more screen on time each day.

00:04:52.689 --> 00:04:55.099
Now lets touch on the ultrasonic fingerprint
reader.

00:04:55.099 --> 00:04:59.270
The tech is super cool, and we couldn’t
fool it in our fingerprint hacking video.

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:00.979
Actually using it was a hit or miss.

00:05:00.979 --> 00:05:05.979
I tried different pressures, angles, lengths
to leave my finger on, it just wasn’t consistent.

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:10.189
I then thought to try and add my print again
and it worked much better!

00:05:10.189 --> 00:05:13.529
The next day Lew put out a video on this and
I was glad it wasn’t just me.

00:05:13.529 --> 00:05:15.509
I added a third print and it got even better.

00:05:15.509 --> 00:05:17.999
It’s still not perfect, but better than
before.

00:05:17.999 --> 00:05:21.749
I think Samsung can tweak this over time and
I know the tech will improve in the future

00:05:21.749 --> 00:05:23.909
but for now it's definitely not as easy as
face ID.

00:05:23.909 --> 00:05:25.270
Other than face ID, the only other hardware
feature I missed is the physical silent switch.

00:05:25.270 --> 00:05:28.729
I love being able to change this quickly even
if the phone is in my pocket and knowing if

00:05:28.729 --> 00:05:30.214
the phone is silent by feeling the switch
or looking at it.

00:05:30.214 --> 00:05:31.214
Come on Samsung, replace your Bixby button
for this.

00:05:31.214 --> 00:05:32.214
I also don't love the curved edges.

00:05:32.214 --> 00:05:33.214
Yes, it looks great for product shots and
makes the phone slimmer so its more comfortable

00:05:33.214 --> 00:05:38.169
to use in the hand but I would often accidentally
change youtube videos and like random Instagram

00:05:38.169 --> 00:05:39.169
photos.

00:05:39.169 --> 00:05:44.750
Personally, I prefer the standard flat design
of the S10e.

00:05:44.750 --> 00:05:46.801
So we talked a lot about hardware, now lets
touch on software.

00:05:46.801 --> 00:05:51.939
The new OneUI is an improvement from the past
but Samsung still has a way to go with speed

00:05:51.939 --> 00:05:54.189
and reliability compared to One Plus.

00:05:54.189 --> 00:05:59.529
I ended up changing my icons and keyboard
when everything one my 6T is great out of

00:05:59.529 --> 00:06:08.779
the box, and that's the beauty of Android,
but iOS has fewer app crashes, glitches, and

00:06:08.779 --> 00:06:09.779
bloatware.

00:06:09.779 --> 00:06:13.589
Notifications on the S10 were annoying with
games trying to get me to play, apps wanting

00:06:13.589 --> 00:06:16.250
to be downloaded, and Amazon wanting me to
shop.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:19.930
All of this can be fixed, but with the iPhone,
you don’t have to.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:24.159
On the plus side, I’m always surprised by
the extra features I noticed in apps I used

00:06:24.159 --> 00:06:25.159
most often.

00:06:25.159 --> 00:06:29.550
I love facebook messengers overlay, and youtubes
picture in picture.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:35.419
So why did I end up changing back?

00:06:35.419 --> 00:06:38.199
It's basically the whole Apple ecosystem holding
me in.

00:06:38.199 --> 00:06:42.180
If it wasn’t, I would switch, but I love
my apple watch and having continuity with

00:06:42.180 --> 00:06:43.180
my Macs.

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:46.939
I use airdrop almost daily, and Force touch
really speeds things up for me.

00:06:46.939 --> 00:06:51.379
Along with that, I didn’t realize how much
losing iMessage would affect me.

00:06:51.379 --> 00:06:55.240
Apple is great at making their products work
seamlessly which is nice but it also sucks

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:56.339
because it locks you in.

00:06:56.339 --> 00:07:00.470
If I didn't need MacOS every day for work,
and didn’t own and love the Apple watch,

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:02.009
I would not have switched back to the iPhone.

00:07:02.009 --> 00:07:05.309
The S10+ is, in my opinion, the best phone
on the market.

00:07:05.309 --> 00:07:07.789
It's not perfect but its the closest you can
get to it.

00:07:07.789 --> 00:07:11.779
If you’re an iPhone user that's not locked
in and thinking of switching, do it, and if

00:07:11.779 --> 00:07:14.689
you’re using Android already and want to
upgrade, it’s a no brainer.

00:07:14.689 --> 00:07:17.940
Thanks for watching, if you want to see more
video like this one, including our Galaxy

00:07:17.940 --> 00:07:23.509
S10e review click the circle to subscribe
and check out our other S10+ vids including

00:07:23.509 --> 00:07:24.509
these ones.

00:07:24.509 --> 00:07:33.049
This has been Max and I’ll see you in the
next video.

